---
// A between-seals leak test on a radial joint: the port, the test volume (including the line and the gauge), and where
// a leak of each seal goes.
const ink = 'var(--rd-ink)', muted = 'var(--rd-muted)', steel = 'var(--rd-steel)', blue = 'var(--rd-blue)', ok = 'var(--rd-ok)', accent = 'var(--rd-accent)';
---

<figure class="viz leakport">
  <p class="viz-title">Testing the space between two seals</p>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 360 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="leakport-desc" style="max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <desc id="leakport-desc">
      A section through a joint with two O-rings. A port drilled through the outer part reaches the space between the
      seals and connects through a line to a gauge, a temperature sensor and a valve on the gas supply. The test volume
      is the space between the seals plus the port, the line and the gauge. A leak of the primary seal goes into the
      case and is seen only by the pressure decay. A leak of the secondary seal goes to the outside, where a helium hood
      or sniffer can also find it.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="lp-arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="context-stroke"></path></marker>
    </defs>
    <rect x="20" y="100" width="270" height="40" fill={steel} fill-opacity="0.45"></rect>
    <rect x="20" y="144" width="270" height="40" fill={steel} fill-opacity="0.3"></rect>
    <text x="28" y="116" font-size="10" fill={ink}>case or housing</text>
    <text x="28" y="178" font-size="10" fill={ink}>closure spigot</text>
    {[110, 200].map((x) => (
      <g>
        <rect x={x - 10} y="144" width="20" height="16" fill="var(--rd-panel)"></rect>
        <circle cx={x} cy="148" r="7" fill={ink} fill-opacity="0.75"></circle>
      </g>
    ))}
    <rect x="117" y="140" width="76" height="4" fill={blue} fill-opacity="0.6"></rect>
    <rect x="152" y="40" width="6" height="100" fill={blue} fill-opacity="0.6"></rect>
    <line x1="158" y1="43" x2="250" y2="43" stroke={blue} stroke-width="5" stroke-opacity="0.6"></line>
    <circle cx="200" cy="43" r="11" fill="var(--rd-panel)" stroke={ink}></circle>
    <line x1="200" y1="43" x2="206" y2="36" stroke={ink} stroke-width="1.5"></line>
    <text x="200" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={ink}>gauge</text>
    <rect x="226" y="52" width="10" height="16" rx="2" fill={muted}></rect>
    <text x="231" y="80" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={muted}>T</text>
    <path d="M250,35 L266,51 L266,35 L250,51 Z" fill="var(--rd-panel)" stroke={ink}></path>
    <text x="258" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={ink}>valve</text>
    <line x1="320" y1="43" x2="268" y2="43" stroke={ink} stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#lp-arr)"></line>
    <text x="322" y="47" font-size="10" fill={ink}>gas</text>
    <text x="110" y="208" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={ink}>primary</text>
    <text x="200" y="208" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={ink}>secondary</text>
    <line x1="98" y1="142" x2="58" y2="142" stroke={accent} stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#lp-arr)"></line>
    <line x1="212" y1="142" x2="320" y2="142" stroke={ok} stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#lp-arr)"></line>
    <rect x="296" y="112" width="58" height="60" rx="4" fill="none" stroke={ok} stroke-dasharray="4 3"></rect>
    <text x="325" y="186" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill={ok}>hood</text>
    <text x="6" y="226" font-size="10" fill={accent}>← into the case: seen by decay only</text>
    <text x="354" y="242" text-anchor="end" font-size="10" fill={ok}>to the outside: decay and hood →</text>
    <text x="164" y="94" font-size="10" fill={blue}>test volume</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The test volume (blue) is the space between the seals plus the port, the line and the gauge. Keep the line short:
    the smaller the volume, the larger the pressure change for the same leak. The test pressure pushes the primary seal
    from its back, opposite to service.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
